From michael.watson at bbsrc.ac.uk  Wed Nov  4 10:39:55 2009
From: michael.watson at bbsrc.ac.uk (michael watson (IAH-C))
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2009 09:39:55 +0000
Subject: [BioC] hclust to newick format?
Message-ID: <8D08960C647E64438CE5740657CBBDC5014875B26C@iahcexch1.iah.bbsrc.ac.uk>

Hello

I am asking the bioC list as it is more likely to contain biologists tha R-help!

Has anyone written any code to convert an hclust object to newick format?

For those of you who don't know, newick is a simple tree representation format used extensively in phylogenetic analysis:

(B:6.0,(A:5.0,C:3.0,E:4.0):5.0,D:11.0);

I am looking to see if certain statistical properties can be used in hclust which will mirror a phylogenetic tree based on DNA sequence, and for that I want to use some of the phylogenetic tree drawing tools on my hclust data, all of which accept newick as standard

Thanks in advance

Mick


From sanjay.bhatikar at biobase-international.com  Wed Nov  4 10:43:48 2009
