>Dear list,
>I would like to know if it is possible to export to excel files the 
>result of a contrast (limma) using OneChannelGUI. I only could export 
>normalized data, but not all the values given by limma (p-value, M, B, etc).
>Thanks,
>Javier


Dear  Javier,
You cannot export the limma results using the graphical interface.
I will make an extra function to extract those data from the graphical 
interface.
In the mean time, you can extract them
from the list in the affylmGUIenvironment environment:
affylmGUIenvironment$ContrastParameterizationList
Cheers
Raffaele



