From: tstraub at med.uni-muenchen.de (Tobias Straub)
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2009 09:15:19 +0100
Subject: [BioC] Is there a package or a way to convert "probesets" to
	"genes"
In-Reply-To: <32dc3df20911161501i7f0c3bacrdf501a352bf4811@mail.gmail.com>
References: <32dc3df20911161501i7f0c3bacrdf501a352bf4811@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <2AA474D0-F8F1-4379-BA94-7CBF1BD0E1A8@med.uni-muenchen.de>

hi richie,

one easy way to handle the multiple probesets per gene problem is to  
keep only the one probeset with the highest variance across  
replicates. the 'nsFilter' function in the 'genefilter' package  
provides this operation for ExpressionSet objects.
using this filter approach you might of course miss some  
differentially regulated splicing events.

best regards
tobias


